                "evidence": "I couldn't find any practitioner regrets about Tailwind v5. Searching turned up only the official announcement.\n\n**What the sources say**\n- The announcement (tailwindcss.com/blog/tailwindcss-v5, published 2026-08-20) lists these changes:\n  - Configuration is CSS-first by default, and the JavaScript config has been removed.\n  - Container queries have new defaults.\n  - The build engine is now Lightning CSS.\n  - There is an upgrade tool: `npx @tailwindcss/upgrade@5`.\n- Four searches across Exa and Tavily, including date-limited ones aimed at blogs, forums, Reddit, Hacker News and GitHub issues, returned that one page every time. I found no first-hand accounts of regret, no migration post-mortems, and no issue threads.\n\n**Inference, not sourced:** The removal of the JS config is the most likely source of migration pain. Projects with JS-based plugins or shared config presets would have to rewrite them. The new container query defaults could also change layouts quietly. Nothing I found confirms either one, so treat both as hypotheses to check.\n\n**What's missing**\n- The vault had no pages on Tailwind.\n- The social lane is missing: `last30days` isn't installed, and I didn't imitate it with a few web searches. That lane is the one most likely to surface real regrets.\n- I didn't search GitHub issues directly with Firecrawl, which could be a useful next step.\n- I haven't written anything to the vault. The evidence is a single announcement page, and I'd rather not save a thin page as if it were a conclusion.\n\n**Coverage:** vault: searched, empty. Web: Exa and Tavily both returned only the official post. Social: `last30days` not installed. Code and issues: not searched. Spend: free tiers only.\n\nIf you'd like, I can search GitHub issues through Firecrawl for v5 migration complaints. If you tell me your stack, such as JS plugins, a shared config or a component library, I can also check the v5 upgrade docs for the parts that affect you."
              }
            ]
